**Ethical reflection — what are the risks of your tool? Who could it harm?**

ArtLab is intended to make art education more accessible, but it has limitations. Its educational content may not suit every learning style or accessibility need, and users with limited internet or device access may still be excluded. Incorrect artwork information, missing image credits, or copyrighted images used without appropriate permission could misinform users or infringe artists' rights. Because the target audience includes minors, collecting unnecessary personal information or exposing saved creative work could also create privacy risks. The prototype therefore aims to minimise data collection, avoid mandatory accounts, and keep progress and journal entries in local browser storage. However, local storage on a shared device is not completely private. ArtLab has not yet demonstrated measurable improvements in learning, so it would need to be tested with students before making claims about its educational impact.

